ack dead-code:new-symbol 9abc6f468bb034db 0 cid=9968d7d6f7ae1c48 Ticket 22 put a second lifecycle beside tunneld's: sandbox.Host accepts local connections, drops them on Close and pushes policy the way Tunneld accepts tunnels, drops them on Close and answers exchanges. Every row here pairs one of that contract's small bodies with an existing one of the same idiomatic shape - a mutex-guarded accessor, a constructor of a struct holding an empty map, a select on a channel or a context, an accept loop - and none of them can share code, because the two members either live in packages that must not import each other (attest/sandbox imports nothing from gvisor.dev/gvisor/attest, which is the import-graph form of the contract's invariant that a sandbox sees no evidence, no key and no trust decision) or sit one in a _test.go file and one outside it. Every member was resolved to its definition before this entry was written. Two rows are the residue of fixes rather than unmade ones: Exchange | OpenStream is what is left after the preamble and the lost-tunnel postamble the two verbs shared were extracted into Channel.tunnelTo and Channel.lost, which took the group from 151 tokens to 48 and left four lines that call different methods on the same connection; LoadPolicyFile | readFrame is what is left after readFrame was split into readHeader and readFramePayload, which is what lets Conn.Serve tell a raw stream from an exchange by the four bytes it opens with. The dead-code row on tunnel.Listen carries was=0 now=0 and names a function tunneld.New calls on every start (attest/tunneld/tunneld.go, the tunnel.Listen call); nothing about its reachability changed in this ticket.
